# Rotation for the two logs the front panel service writes. See newsyslog.conf(5).
#
# These are ordinary files rather than syslog because the settings page reads the LCDd log
# back: what the driver last reported is the only honest answer to "has a key on this panel
# ever been pressed", and a file is something a script can tail. LCDd is nearly silent at its
# usual reporting level, but the key test raises that level on purpose, and a panel whose keys
# are polled several times a second can then write a great deal in an afternoon - hence a size
# limit rather than a schedule.
#
# The signal goes to the daemon(8) supervisor named in the pidfile, not to LCDd or to the
# client: daemon is what holds the log open, and it was started with -H so that SIGHUP means
# "close this file and open it again" and nothing else. Neither program is disturbed.
#
# The two names are the ones the rest of the plugin uses: LCDd.log is where keys.py looks for
# what the driver reported, client.log is the screen client's own, and the pidfiles are the
# supervisors daemon(8) writes. 600 is daemon(8)'s own mode for a file it creates, so the entry
# and the file agree on the first rotation as well as on the fiftieth.
#
# The third file is the service's own account of every start and stop it was asked for, and
# it is the odd one out twice over. N, because nothing holds it open: each line is a separate
# append by the rc script, so there is no process to tell about the rotation - and without N
# newsyslog would send SIGHUP to syslogd for want of anything better to signal. And a much
# smaller size, because the whole value of the file is that one boot can be read straight
# through: at a dozen lines per start it would take years to reach even this.
#
# logfilename                        [owner:group]  mode  count  size  when  flags  [/pid_file]                              [sig_num]
/var/log/frontpanel/LCDd.log         root:wheel     600   4      200   *     CJ     /var/run/frontpanel/LCDd.supervisor.pid   1
/var/log/frontpanel/client.log       root:wheel     600   4      200   *     CJ     /var/run/frontpanel/client.supervisor.pid 1
/var/log/frontpanel/trace.log        root:wheel     600   2      50    *     CJN
